We return to the example of the cone of radius a and height h and, this time, use spherical coordinates to calculate its volume. 
First, note two things: (i) that the cone's lateral surface has the equation φ = tan^(-1) (a/h) in a spherical coordinates and (ii) that the planar top having Cartesian equation z = h has spherical equation p cos(φ) = h or, equivalently, p = h sec(φ)
(See Figure 5.105)

